## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical NLP pipeline setup, handling class imbalance, and real-world deployment concerns for a beginner-friendly problem.

## Key Concepts
- TF-IDF vectorization with unigrams/bigrams
- Handling imbalanced data via class_weight
- Time-based train/test splits to mimic streaming data
- Evaluation: macro F1 and PR-AUC for imbalanced tasks
- Canary rollout and monitoring basics for production safety

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: outline of pipeline components
function buildPipeline(){
  const vectorizer = new TFIDF({ngramRange:[1,2], maxFeatures:100000});
  const model = new LogisticRegression({classWeight:'balanced'});
  return {vectorizer, model};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to multi-class categorization of spam types?
- How would you monitor drift and adjust thresholds in production?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests designing a practical, on-device ML flow that balances accuracy, size, privacy, and deployment realities.

## Key Concepts
- On-device constraints: memory, CPU, quantization
- Feature engineering: cyclical time, geospatial bucketing, hashed categories
- Model choice: compact linear models with proper regularization
- Privacy-aware validation: leave-one-user-out or per-session splits
- Evaluation: AUROC, calibration, appropriate thresholds

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tiny logistic regression dot-product (illustrative)
function predict(w, x) {
  let s = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < w.length; i++) s += w[i] * x[i];
  return 1 / (1 + Math.exp(-s));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle missing values on-device?
- How would you validate robustness to distribution shifts after deployment?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess edge ML design at scale: latency, privacy, drift, and device heterogeneity in a warehouse setting.

## Key Concepts

- Edge inference optimization (quantization, pruning)
- Federated learning and secure aggregation
- Concept drift detection and continual learning
- Monitoring, rollout, and rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: edge inference entry
function infer(frame, model) {
  const input = preprocess(frame);
  const out = model.run(input);
  return postprocess(out);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate privacy guarantees end-to-end?
- What failure modes impact latency and how mitigate them?
